.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH wx-metar 1  "metar " 
.SH NAME
wx\-metar \- Current conditions from the nearest METAR station, from aviationweather.gov
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBwx metar\fR [\fB\-s\fR|\fB\-\-style\fR] [\fB\-t\fR|\fB\-\-temp\-unit\fR] [\fB\-\-raw\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIPLACE\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Current conditions from the nearest METAR station, from aviationweather.gov
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-style\fR \fI<STYLE>\fR [default: full]
How to word the announcement
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
full: The full announcement, with the station\*(Aqs name
.IP \(bu 2
brief: Brief announcement format, without the station name
.IP \(bu 2
detailed: Detailed weather report
.IP \(bu 2
aviation: Aviation radio style
.RE
.TP
\fB\-t\fR, \fB\-\-temp\-unit\fR \fI<TEMP_UNIT>\fR [default: fahrenheit]
Temperature unit (the detailed style always gives both)
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
fahrenheit
.IP \(bu 2
celsius
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-raw\fR
Print the raw METAR instead of an announcement
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIPLACE\fR>
A station (KSJC), latitude,longitude, US street address or place name ("Mountain View, CA"); quotes are optional
